```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main()
{
    char name[100];
    int rollNumber;
    char section;
    int age;
    float cgpa;
    double height;

    printf("Enter student name: ");
    fgets(name, sizeof(name), stdin);

    printf("Enter roll number: ");
    scanf("%d", &rollNumber);

    printf("Enter section: ");
    scanf(" %c", &section);

    printf("Enter age: ");
    scanf("%d", &age);

    printf("Enter CGPA: ");
    scanf("%f", &cgpa);

    printf("Enter height: ");
    scanf("%lf", &height);

    printf("\n========================================\n");
    printf("\t\tSTUDENT REPORT\n");
    printf("========================================\n");

    printf("Field\t\tValue\n");
    printf("----------------------------------------\n");

    printf("Name\t\t%s", name);
    printf("Roll Number\t%d\n", rollNumber);
    printf("Section\t\t%c\n", section);
    printf("Age\t\t%d\n", age);
    printf("CGPA\t\t%.2f\n", cgpa);
    printf("Height\t\t%.2lf\n", height);

    printf("----------------------------------------\n");

    return 0;
}
```

### 📁 File name

**`Task9_FormattedStudentReport.c`**

### What this task demonstrates

* `char[]` → Student name
* `int` → Roll number and age
* `char` → Section
* `float` → CGPA
* `double` → Height
* `%s` → String
* `%d` → Integer
* `%c` → Character
* `%.2f` → CGPA with 2 decimal places
* `%.2lf` → Height with 2 decimal places
* `\t` → Tabs
* `\n` → New lines
